\details{
\strong{Two-stage delta and bounded formulas.} For stage Jacobians \eqn{H_c, H_s},
anchor map \eqn{A = \partial a/\partial b_c}, cross-derivative \eqn{B}, and
target derivatives \eqn{G_s, G_a}, union-event loadings are
\eqn{U_s = X_s H_s^{-1}G_s^\top} and
\eqn{U_c = X_c H_c^{-1}A^\top(G_a - G_s H_s^{-1}B)^\top} with categorical
covariance \eqn{V = \sum_e \mathrm{Cov}_{p_{g,e}}(U_s + U_c)} (Murphy &
Topel, 1985; \code{CIEligible = FALSE} pending short-exposure qualification). For
\code{"bounded"}, signed event weights \eqn{a_e} on scores in \eqn{[l, u]} have
Hoeffding radius \eqn{r = \sqrt{\tfrac12\log(2/\alpha)\sum_e a_e^2(u - l)^2}}
(\code{CIEligible = TRUE}, \code{Informative} flags bounds narrower than the full
rubric range; Hoeffding, 1963).

\code{plot()} method: Plot common-plan expected-score intervals

For \code{plot()}: Points are common-plan expected scores or declared paired differences.
Bars show only available pointwise bounds under the saved method. Missing
bars are not zero uncertainty. Plotting never recalculates the fit or removes
unresolved rows from the saved result. For refit results the bars show the
empirical interval; endpoint Monte Carlo enclosures are retained in the
returned table and \code{plot_data(p)$monte_carlo}, not drawn as sampling intervals. See
\code{\link[=confint.mfrm_fair_average]{confint.mfrm_fair_average()}} for
the estimand, assumptions and finite-sample limitations.

Computes model-adjusted reference averages in score units across \code{by_facet},
\code{stacked}, and unformatted \code{raw_by_facet} (\code{Level} key). \code{RSM} uses the
shared scale; \code{PCM} converts each observation's reference predictor using its
administered step profile before weight-averaging (\code{Fair(M)} /
\code{AdjustedAverage} sets other facets to their finite means; \code{Fair(Z)} /
\code{StandardizedAdjustedAverage} sets them to zero, which is an expected score
at zero reference rather than a z-score).

\strong{Extreme-score handling (\code{xtreme > 0})}: \code{PrimaryMeasure} retains the
original fitted measure. \code{"display"} inverts an endpoint-shifted average for
\code{Measure} only (\verb{Model S.E.} is \code{NA}; fair averages are unchanged). For
ordinary additive RSM/PCM JML without group-mean anchors, \code{"facets"} shifts
the eligible weighted total inward by \code{xtreme} times the smallest positive
weight (retaining finite direct anchors unless paired with an unanchored
extreme), solves the conditional score equation, and reports conditional
reciprocal-sqrt-information SE (\code{MeasureBasis}, \code{MeasureSEBasis},
\code{ExtremeAdjustment}). Fair-score CIs remain unavailable when \code{xtreme > 0}.

\strong{GPCM and SE caveat}: For slope-facet element \eqn{j^\star},
\deqn{\mathrm{FA}_{p, j^\star} = \sum_k k \cdot P_{GPCM}(X = k \mid \theta_p, a_{j^\star}, \boldsymbol{\delta}_{j^\star});}
non-slope facets use unit geometric-mean slope and average threshold profiles
before conversion (a package reporting convention, not FACETS score-side
equivalence). \verb{Model S.E.} / \code{ModelBasedSE} and \verb{Real S.E.} / \code{FitAdjustedSE}
are \strong{measure-level} SEs rescaled by \code{abs(uscale)} -- never use them as
\eqn{\pm 1.96\,\mathrm{SE}} bounds on fair scores. When \code{fair_se = TRUE} on
MML GPCM fits, structural delta-method \verb{Fair(M) S.E.} / \code{AdjustedAverageSE}
columns are added for non-Person facets (\code{Person} rows stay \code{NA};
\code{FairCIEligible = FALSE}, diagnostic use only).
}
